.TH MEMORY-BUS 7 "May 2026" "v1.0" "Sovereign Mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
memory-bus \- High-speed zero-copy RAM teleportation bus
.SH DESCRIPTION
The **Memory Bus** (Port 11111) enables high-speed virtual agent teleportation using POSIX shared memory maps (\fBmmap\fR). This eliminates serialization latency by allowing agents to write state buffers directly into RAM pages.
.SH ARCHITECTURE
The system uses a $64\text{MB}$ memory buffer block inside the volatile shared memory filesystem at \fB/dev/shm/sovereign_page_table\fR.
.SS Operation
.IP 1.
\fBMemory Seeding:\fR The bus server initializes the page table in \fB/dev/shm/\fR.
.IP 2.
\fBPage Allocation:\fR Teleporting agents query Port 11111 for a memory slot.
.IP 3.
\fBZero-Copy Access:\fR Agents receive a direct pointer to the RAM segment for instant read/write operations without CPU serialization overhead.
.IP 4.
\fBFailover:\fR If hypervisor links drop, the bus falls back to standard TCP streams.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB/dev/shm/sovereign_page_table\fR
The underlying POSIX shared memory page file.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBstarbirth\fR(7), \fBjetweb\fR(7), \fBmesh_control.sh\fR(1)
